# Copy values into your process environment; Spring does not automatically load this file.
# Provision a dedicated MySQL 8+ utf8mb4 database first. No H2 or credential defaults exist.
DB_URL=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/hive_importer
DB_USERNAME=replace_with_dedicated_database_user
DB_PASSWORD=replace_with_database_password
PORT=8080
APP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# Optional bounded public-demo quotas.
APP_MAX_WORKSPACES=500
APP_MAX_TEMPLATES_PER_WORKSPACE=10
APP_MAX_COMMENTS_PER_WORKSPACE=25000
APP_WORKSPACE_REQUESTS_PER_HOUR=10
APP_IMPORT_REQUESTS_PER_HOUR=20

# Real-MySQL integration tests run only when all three TEST_DB_* environment
# variables are supplied. Without them, Maven explicitly reports these tests skipped.
# Use an isolated test database, never production or ATSRadar. Tests create/delete
# only their own workspaces; Flyway installs the schema in this dedicated database.
# TEST_DB_URL=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/hive_importer_test
# TEST_DB_USERNAME=replace_with_dedicated_test_user
# TEST_DB_PASSWORD=replace_with_test_database_password
#
# On Windows, select an installed Java 21 JAVA_HOME before .\mvnw.cmd test.
# Build ../frontend first (npm ci, then npm run build). Maven copies frontend/dist
# into BOOT-INF/classes/static, so the executable JAR serves the React index at /
# and the existing API at /api. Real-MySQL integration tests also verify that
# bundle, its scripts/styles, and API isolation. No client-side router fallback is
# needed. Rebuild frontend before packaging backend whenever frontend changes.
# Page CSP permits same-origin scripts, styles and images (plus data images),
# React inline styles, and HTTP(S) API connections to retain optional
# VITE_API_BASE_URL builds. No inline scripts, eval, frames or objects are allowed.
# API responses retain their strict default-src 'none' policy. CORS is applied
# only to /api/*; configure APP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS with the public Azure site origin.
#
# The rate guard is in-memory per instance, using the direct socket address only
# (not X-Forwarded-For). Workspace/template/comment quotas are transactional in MySQL.
# Clearing a browser token does not delete its workspace; demo cleanup is an
# administrator concern. Do not upload actual customer data.
#
# Parser limits: 10 MiB upload, 5,000 worksheet rows including header, 256 columns,
# 200,000 physical cells, 16 sheets with exactly one nonempty data sheet,
# 32,767 characters/cell, 256 characters/header, 8 MiB source-value characters,
# 16 MiB expanded metadata characters, 1,024 ZIP entries, 16 MiB/entry,
# 50 MiB expanded archive, maximum 100:1 compression ratio, two concurrent parses.
# OOXML XML preflight also limits nesting to 64, shared strings to 200,000 and
# styles to 10,000; external entities and duplicate coordinates are rejected.
# Legacy BIFF row/cell limits are checked with a streaming event pass before POI
# builds its object model. XML/ZIP preflight similarly precedes OOXML allocation.
# Excel formula/error cells and macro-enabled OOXML are rejected without evaluation.
# Edit requests are capped at 16 MiB; template names at 255 characters,
# section/item/comment names at 512 and edited comment bodies at 65,535.
